  "live_records": {
    "q-42053": {
      "dom_id": "step-q42053",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨1,2,4⟩$, $b=⟨3,5,-7⟩$ and $c=⟨1,0,2⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(5\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-7))-2(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-7))+4(3\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =10-26-20 \\\\  & =-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|-36|=36.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
