    "q-42055": {
      "dom_id": "step-q42055",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-1,2,5⟩$, $b=⟨1,-4,2⟩$ and $c=⟨0,5,1⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-((-4)\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 2)-2(1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 2)+5(1\\cdot 5-0\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =14-2+25 \\\\  & =37\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|37|=37.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
