    "q-18262": {
      "dom_id": "step-q18262",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $p=⟨0,1,-1⟩$, $q=⟨-2,3,1⟩$ and $r=⟨-1,4,3⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-((-2)\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 1)-((-2)\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =5+5 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|10|=10.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
