    "q-280710": {
      "dom_id": "step-q280710",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $a=⟨4,0,2⟩$, $b=⟨1,3,0⟩$, and $c=⟨0,2,5⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(3\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 2)+0+2(1\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =60+0+4 \\\\  & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|64|=64.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
