    "q-280722": {
      "dom_id": "step-q280722",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨1,3,0⟩$, $b=⟨0,4,2⟩$, and $c=⟨2,k,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\na\\cdot (b\\times c)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k & 5\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ k & 5\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 5-2\\cdot k)-3(0\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 2)=(20-2k)+12 \\\\  & =32-2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 32-2k & =0 \\\\ -2k & =-32 \\\\ k & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=16.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
