    "q-280323": {
      "dom_id": "step-q280323",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(1,1,1),$ $B(2,3,4),$ $C(-1,2,0),$ and $D(3,0,5).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+3j+4k)-(i+j+k) \\\\  & =i+2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j)-(i+j+k) \\\\  & =-2i+j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i+5k)-(i+j+k) \\\\  & =2i-j+4k \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot (-1))-2((-2)\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot 2)+3((-2)\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =1(4-1)-2(-8+2)+3(2-2) \\\\  & =3+12+0 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|15|=15.\n$$",
