    "q-20144": {
      "dom_id": "step-q20144",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(3,-2,2)$, $B(4,3,2)$, $C(1,3,5)$, $D(2,4,-6).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i+3j+2k)-(3i-2j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+3j+5k)-(3i-2j+2k) \\\\  & =-2i+5j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-2,5,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+4j-6k)-(3i-2j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+6j-8k \\\\  & =⟨-1,6,-8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 6 & -8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -8\\end{aligned}|-5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -8\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(5\\cdot (-8)-6\\cdot 3)-5((-2)\\cdot (-8)-(-1)\\cdot 3)+0 \\\\  & =-58-95 \\\\  & =-153.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-153|=153.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
