    "q-128471": {
      "dom_id": "step-q128471",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(0,9,4),$ $B(3,8,2),$ $C(2,9,1),$ and $D(-1,7,7).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+8j+2k)-(9j+4k) \\\\  & =3i-j-2k \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(2i+9j+k)-(9j+4k) \\\\  & =2i-3k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(-i+7j+7k)-(9j+4k) \\\\  & =-i-2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(0\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot (-3))+(2\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot (-3))-2(2\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-18+3+8 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-7|=7.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
