    "q-281027": {
      "dom_id": "step-q281027",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(3,1,2),$ $B(0,5,0),$ $C(3,3,1),$ and $D(1,4,2).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(5j)-(3i+1j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+4j-2k \\\\  & =⟨-3,4,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+3j+1k)-(3i+1j+2k) \\\\  & =2j-1k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(1i+4j+2k)-(3i+1j+2k) \\\\  & =-2i+3j \\\\  & =⟨-2,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(2\\cdot 0-(-1)(3))-4(0\\cdot 0-(-1)(-2))+(-2)(0\\cdot 3-2\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-3(3)-4(-2)-2(4) \\\\  & =-9-8+8 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-9|=9.\n$$",
